[{:db/id 17592186124449 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-08ef8961-263a-5251-a28f-91bd26031d10" "question-923e8280-3481-5e90-8081-225a78ef2cea"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-08ef8961-263a-5251-a28f-91bd26031d10" :question/id #uuid "08ef8961-263a-5251-a28f-91bd26031d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-36523" :question/problem "Consider that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first, second and third-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ What is the value of ${f}_{yxy}(1,0)-{f}_{yy}(1,0)-{f}_{xyy}(1,0)$ given that ${f}_{yy}(x,y)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡xy?$" :question/worked-solution "As the function and its first, second, and third-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ we must have ${f}_{yxy}(x,y)={f}_{xyy}(x,y).$ \n\nTherefore, we can swap the order of the subscripts in the first term. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxy}(1,0)-{f}_{yy}(1,0)-{f}_{xyy}(1,0) & ={f}_{xyy}(1,0)-{f}_{yy}(1,0)-{f}_{xyy}(1,0) \\\\  & =\\cancel{{f}_{xyy}(1,0)}-{f}_{yy}(1,0)-\\cancel{{f}_{xyy}(1,0)} \\\\  & =-{f}_{yy}(1,0) \\\\  & =-(1)^{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c178518b-a0fe-5bb1-9ccb-2e562d423be4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c178518b-a0fe-5bb1-9ccb-2e562d423be4" :answer-field/id #uuid "c178518b-a0fe-5bb1-9ccb-2e562d423be4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b6d893f9-d5e3-5e3f-8ad1-b21394af5064" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b6d893f9-d5e3-5e3f-8ad1-b21394af5064" "answer-70500de8-c6d4-538a-a490-a042ef069ca3" "answer-92afcd1e-56b0-514b-aa96-d6441ab63941" "answer-5c1bdf62-5e9d-55fa-82ff-dab50af9bc96" "answer-4a2bcb36-868f-5f54-a6d3-5044da4b78ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6d893f9-d5e3-5e3f-8ad1-b21394af5064" :answer/id #uuid "b6d893f9-d5e3-5e3f-8ad1-b21394af5064" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70500de8-c6d4-538a-a490-a042ef069ca3" :answer/id #uuid "70500de8-c6d4-538a-a490-a042ef069ca3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92afcd1e-56b0-514b-aa96-d6441ab63941" :answer/id #uuid "92afcd1e-56b0-514b-aa96-d6441ab63941" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c1bdf62-5e9d-55fa-82ff-dab50af9bc96" :answer/id #uuid "5c1bdf62-5e9d-55fa-82ff-dab50af9bc96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a2bcb36-868f-5f54-a6d3-5044da4b78ba" :answer/id #uuid "4a2bcb36-868f-5f54-a6d3-5044da4b78ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-923e8280-3481-5e90-8081-225a78ef2cea" :question/id #uuid "923e8280-3481-5e90-8081-225a78ef2cea" :question/math-academy-id "q-133393" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{zxz}(2,\\frac{1}{2},1)$ given that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ and that\n\n$$\n{f}_{zz}(x,y,z)=2z\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+x{e}^{z-2y}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zzx}(x,y,z) & ={f}_{zxz}(x,y,z) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{zz}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2z\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+x{e}^{z-2y}) \\\\  & =2z\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-2y}+{e}^{z-2y} \\\\  & =\\frac{2z}{x-2y}+{e}^{z-2y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point  $(2,\\frac{1}{2},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zxz}(2,\\frac{1}{2},1) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{2-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}}+{e}^{1-2\\cdot 1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2-1}+{e}^{1-1} \\\\  & =2+1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-504a276b-9fed-5959-a86c-c2b987992901"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-504a276b-9fed-5959-a86c-c2b987992901" :answer-field/id #uuid "504a276b-9fed-5959-a86c-c2b987992901" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-59fd5070-c975-5965-b9d4-d62ba5834853" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d58c242-f6fd-5d67-8e96-0273fcae35a5" "answer-45730328-f0dc-5c33-a6c2-53d71d04445d" "answer-4421a8c6-aea6-5d62-9cd0-8a06f8915dcd" "answer-59fd5070-c975-5965-b9d4-d62ba5834853" "answer-d26ca855-4a28-50fd-bba1-040fec87c89e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d58c242-f6fd-5d67-8e96-0273fcae35a5" :answer/id #uuid "4d58c242-f6fd-5d67-8e96-0273fcae35a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45730328-f0dc-5c33-a6c2-53d71d04445d" :answer/id #uuid "45730328-f0dc-5c33-a6c2-53d71d04445d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4421a8c6-aea6-5d62-9cd0-8a06f8915dcd" :answer/id #uuid "4421a8c6-aea6-5d62-9cd0-8a06f8915dcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59fd5070-c975-5965-b9d4-d62ba5834853" :answer/id #uuid "59fd5070-c975-5965-b9d4-d62ba5834853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d26ca855-4a28-50fd-bba1-040fec87c89e" :answer/id #uuid "d26ca855-4a28-50fd-bba1-040fec87c89e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3c715a18-b04f-5fa8-b565-cd1d87a53bb9" :activity/id #uuid "3c715a18-b04f-5fa8-b565-cd1d87a53bb9" :activity/title "Equality of Mixed Partial Derivatives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049696 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-87e1e468-067a-5b37-817d-ee60c3d401bf" "